Loop structures in PHP:

1. for loop: Used when number of iterations is known in advance.
Syntax: for (init; condition; increment) { code; }
Example: for ($i=1; $i<=5; $i++) { echo $i; }

2. while loop: Entry-controlled loop executing as long as test condition is true.
Syntax: while (condition) { code; increment; }

3. do...while loop: Exit-controlled loop executing block at least once.
Syntax: do { code; } while (condition);

4. foreach loop: Specifically used to iterate over arrays.
Syntax: foreach ($array as $value) { echo $value; }

The 'foreach' loop in PHP works exclusively on arrays and objects.

1. Syntax for Values only:
foreach ($array as $value) {
    echo $value . " ";
}
Example:
$fruits = array("Apple", "Banana", "Mango");
foreach ($fruits as $fruit) {
    echo $fruit . "<br>";
}

2. Syntax for Key and Value pairs (Associative arrays):
foreach ($array as $key => $value) {
    echo $key . " : " . $value . "<br>";
}
Example:
$marks = array("Tamil" => 95, "English" => 90, "CS" => 99);
foreach ($marks as $subject => $mark) {
    echo "Subject: " . $subject . ", Mark: " . $mark . "<br>";
}

